    "body": "[A10] READINESS RECHECK / DECISION (2026-09-22)\n\nAt current dev b17580b91deb11f3441dfc5d7f9fafe539d929b8, eight synthetic fixtures were compared with GitHub's Markdown API (gfm mode). Each fixture places `## Probe` after the delimiter under test. Counts below are walk / rendered h2; this is a focused readiness check, not the acceptance sweep.\n\n| Position | Counts | Current refusal |\n|---|---|---|\n| fence plus space | 1 / 1 | none |\n| fence plus tab | 1 / 1 | none |\n| fence plus form feed | 1 / 0 | page refused |\n| `<pre>` then `</pre >` | 1 / 0 | none |\n| `<pre>` then `</pre` + tab + `>` | 1 / 0 | none |\n| `<pre>` then `</style>` | 0 / 1 | none |\n| `<pre>` then `</PRE>` | 1 / 1 | none |\n| `<script>` then `</` + U+017F + `cript>` | 0 / 0 | none |\n\nChoose the renderer's exact closing rules, preserving the existing global refusal policy: only space/tab may trail a closing fence; any of the four literal type-1 closing names ends any type-1 block, with ASCII case folding and no internal blank. The cross-name case is already assigned to #440 in `_type_1_end` and the public R86-9 report; it is part of the same end-condition fix. Unicode case folding is already corrected at this dev and must stay corrected.\n\nAuthority: [CommonMark 0.31.2 section 4.5](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#fenced-code-blocks), [section 4.6](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#html-blocks), CONTRIBUTING.md 6.1, and [R86-9 evidence](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/428#issuecomment-5651750010). The issue's full measured-character sweep, carriage-return handling, base/head comparison, per-family mutation sensitivity and documentation remain required. Distinguish the raw walk from the shipped entry points that refuse characters or normalize line endings. Do not relax the refused character population or broaden this into #437's container-state redesign.\n\nNo implementation has started. This task can use the next free author slot without touching #407's CI files or #478's builder files. Assign roles and move to In progress before the first edit.\n",
