    "body": "[A158] TAKEN\nBranch: `440-markdown-closers`, base `b17580b91deb11f3441dfc5d7f9fafe539d929b8`.\nAuthority: REQUIREMENTS section 8 / REQ-VER-04; CONTRIBUTING sections 5, 6.1; code-quality rule 12; CommonMark 0.31.2 sections [4.5](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#fenced-code-blocks) and [4.6](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#html-blocks); issue decisions 5651705425 and 5771170243; [R86-9](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/428#issuecomment-5651750010) and [R85-8](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/428#issuecomment-5651704309). Assignment 5771559992 names A158 / internal R225 / external R226 / manager A10; project is In progress.\nScope: closing fences admit only trailing spaces/tabs; any literal type-1 closer ends any type-1 block, ASCII-folded, with no internal blanks. Preserve global refusal, ASCII folding, precedence, provenance and paragraph/container behavior; #437 stays separate. Reserve `I440` for the new control family; existing controls retain their identities.\nValidation: reconstruct the documented historical character population if its original instruments are not publicly available; run identical synthetic fixtures at base/head against `gh api markdown` in gfm mode, saving exact source and HTML outside tracked Markdown. Measure raw walk, shipped refusal/CR normalization, hidden-heading label rejection, per-property mutations, and per-page classifications/generation. Run gen_toc selftest/check/verify-anchors/sites, check_em_dash selftest/actual-base gate, docs_check, doc paths, Python idiom ratchets, class/source guards. A10 owns complete native gates, trusted act, hosted CI, publication, review orchestration and merge. No push, PR, Docker/act, full milan_dp sweep or subagents in this author lane.\nBlockers: none. The public review reports name local evidence paths but expose no instrument download; the reviewed public tree contains none of those tools. Any reconstructed population will be identified explicitly.\n",
